{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"Kaposi sarcoma is a disease in which malignant tumors (cancer) can form in the skin, mucous membranes, lymph nodes, and other organs.","source_span":"Kaposi sarcoma is a disease in which malignant tumors (cancer) can form in the skin, mucous membranes, lymph nodes, and other organs."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"Human herpesvirus-8 (HHV-8) is found in the lesions of all patients with Kaposi sarcoma.","source_span":"Human herpesvirus-8 (HHV-8) is found in the lesions of all patients with Kaposi sarcoma."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"HHV-8 is also called Kaposi sarcoma herpesvirus (KSHV).","source_span":"This virus is also called Kaposi sarcoma herpesvirus (KSHV)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"People infected with HHV-8 who are most likely to develop Kaposi sarcoma have immune systems weakened by disease or by drugs given after an organ transplant.","source_span":"Those infected with HHV-8 who are most likely to develop Kaposi sarcoma have immune systems weakened by disease or by drugs given after an organ transplant."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"There are several types of Kaposi sarcoma: Classic, African, Immunosuppressive therapy-related, Epidemic, and Nonepidemic Kaposi sarcoma.","source_span":"Classic Kaposi sarcoma. - African Kaposi sarcoma. - Immunosuppressive therapyrelated Kaposi sarcoma. - Epidemic Kaposi sarcoma. - Nonepidemic Kaposi sarcoma."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"A chest x-ray is used to find Kaposi sarcoma in the lungs.","source_span":"This is used to find Kaposi sarcoma in the lungs."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"A lower than normal CD34 lymphocyte count can be a sign that the immune system is not working well.","source_span":"A lower than normal amount of CD34 cells can be a sign the immune system is not working well."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"Prognosis and treatment options for Kaposi sarcoma depend on the type of Kaposi sarcoma, the general health of the patient (especially the immune system), and whether the cancer is newly diagnosed or recurrent.","source_span":"The prognosis (chance of recovery) and treatment options depend on the following: - The type of Kaposi sarcoma. - The general health of the patient, especially the patient's immune system. - Whether the cancer has just been diagnosed or has recurred (come back)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"Classic Kaposi sarcoma is found most often in older men of Italian or Eastern European Jewish origin.","source_span":"Classic Kaposi sarcoma is found most often in older men of Italian or Eastern European Jewish origin."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","statement":"Signs of classic Kaposi sarcoma may include slow-growing lesions on the legs and feet.","source_span":"Signs of classic Kaposi sarcoma may include slow-growing lesions on the legs and feet."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","fact_refs":[1,2],"question":"What virus is found in the lesions of all Kaposi sarcoma patients, and by what other name is it known?","answer":"Human herpesvirus-8 (HHV-8) is found in the lesions of all Kaposi sarcoma patients; it is also called Kaposi sarcoma herpesvirus (KSHV)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What are the five types of Kaposi sarcoma mentioned in the document?","answer":"Classic, African, Immunosuppressive therapy-related, Epidemic, and Nonepidemic Kaposi sarcoma."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","fact_refs":[3],"question":"Among people infected with HHV-8, who is most likely to develop Kaposi sarcoma?","answer":"Those whose immune systems are weakened by disease or by drugs given after an organ transplant are most likely to develop Kaposi sarcoma."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","fact_refs":[8],"question":"Which population is most often affected by classic Kaposi sarcoma?","answer":"Classic Kaposi sarcoma is found most often in older men of Italian or Eastern European Jewish origin."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","fact_refs":[9],"question":"What signs may appear with classic Kaposi sarcoma?","answer":"Signs of classic Kaposi sarcoma may include slow-growing lesions on the legs and feet."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_3","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What three factors affect the prognosis and treatment options for Kaposi sarcoma?","answer":"Prognosis and treatment depend on the type of Kaposi sarcoma, the patient's general health (especially the immune system), and whether the cancer is newly diagnosed or has recurred."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","statement":"Risk factors for childhood rhabdomyosarcoma include the inherited diseases Li-Fraumeni syndrome, pleuropulmonary blastoma, neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1), Costello syndrome, Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome, and Noonan syndrome.","source_span":"Risk factors for rhabdomyosarcoma include having the following inherited diseases: - Li-Fraumeni syndrome. - Pleuropulmonary blastoma. - Neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1). - Costello syndrome. - Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome. - Noonan syndrome."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","statement":"Children who had a high birth weight or were larger than expected at birth may have an increased risk of embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma.","source_span":"Children who had a high birth weight or were larger than expected at birth may have an increased risk of embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","statement":"In most cases, the cause of childhood rhabdomyosarcoma is not known.","source_span":"In most cases, the cause of rhabdomyosarcoma is not known."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","statement":"A sign of childhood rhabdomyosarcoma is a lump or swelling that keeps getting bigger.","source_span":"A sign of childhood rhabdomyosarcoma is a lump or swelling that keeps getting bigger."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","statement":"Symptoms of childhood rhabdomyosarcoma can include bulging of the eye, headache, trouble urinating or having bowel movements, blood in the urine, and bleeding in the nose, throat, vagina, or rectum.","source_span":"Bulging of the eye. - Headache. - Trouble urinating or having bowel movements. - Blood in the urine. - Bleeding in the nose, throat, vagina, or rectum."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","statement":"In a sentinel lymph node biopsy, a radioactive substance and/or blue dye is injected near the tumor and the first lymph node to receive it is removed for examination.","source_span":"A radioactive substance and/or blue dye is injected near the tumor. The substance or dye flows through the lymph ducts to the lymph nodes. The first lymph node to receive the substance or dye is removed."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","statement":"FISH (fluorescence in situ hybridization) is a laboratory test used to look at genes or chromosomes in cells and tissues to find certain gene changes.","source_span":"FISH (fluorescence in situ hybridization): A laboratory test used to look at genes or chromosomes in cells and tissues... This type of test is used to find certain gene changes."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","statement":"Because treatment depends on the type of rhabdomyosarcoma, biopsy samples should be checked by a pathologist who has experience diagnosing rhabdomyosarcoma.","source_span":"Because treatment depends on the type of rhabdomyosarcoma, biopsy samples should be checked by a pathologist who has experience in diagnosing rhabdomyosarcoma."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","fact_refs":[0],"question":"Which inherited diseases are listed as risk factors for childhood rhabdomyosarcoma?","answer":"Li-Fraumeni syndrome, pleuropulmonary blastoma, neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1), Costello syndrome, Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome, and Noonan syndrome."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What birth-related factor may increase a child's risk of embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma?","answer":"Having a high birth weight or being larger than expected at birth may increase the risk of embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What is a common sign of childhood rhabdomyosarcoma?","answer":"A lump or swelling that keeps getting bigger (and may be painful) is a common sign of childhood rhabdomyosarcoma."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Besides a growing lump, what other symptoms can childhood rhabdomyosarcoma cause?","answer":"It can cause bulging of the eye, headache, trouble urinating or having bowel movements, blood in the urine, and bleeding in the nose, throat, vagina, or rectum."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What is injected near the tumor during a sentinel lymph node biopsy, and what happens to the first lymph node that receives it?","answer":"A radioactive substance and/or blue dye is injected near the tumor; the first lymph node to receive the substance or dye is removed and examined under a microscope for cancer cells."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_4","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What does the FISH test look for in diagnosing childhood rhabdomyosarcoma?","answer":"FISH (fluorescence in situ hybridization) examines genes or chromosomes in cells and tissues to find certain gene changes."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","statement":"Childhood soft tissue sarcoma is a disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in soft tissues of the body.","source_span":"Childhood soft tissue sarcoma is a disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in soft tissues of the body."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","statement":"In children, soft tissue sarcoma tumors form most often in the arms, legs, or trunk (chest and abdomen).","source_span":"In children, the tumors form most often in the arms, legs, or trunk (chest and abdomen)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","statement":"Myxoid liposarcoma is usually low grade and responds well to treatment, and its cells have a genetic translocation used to diagnose it.","source_span":"Myxoid liposarcoma is usually low grade and responds well to treatment. The cells of myxoid liposarcoma have a certain genetic change called a translocation... In order to diagnose myxoid liposarcoma, the tumor cells are checked for this genetic change."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","statement":"Pleomorphic liposarcoma is usually high grade (likely to grow and spread quickly) and is less likely to respond well to treatment.","source_span":"Pleomorphic liposarcoma is usually high grade (likely to grow and spread quickly) and is less likely to respond well to treatment."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","statement":"Extraskeletal mesenchymal chondrosarcoma often affects young adults and occurs in the head and neck.","source_span":"Extraskeletal mesenchymal chondrosarcoma. This type of bone and cartilage tumor often affects young adults and occurs in the head and neck."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","statement":"Desmoid tumors sometimes occur in children with changes in the APC gene, which causes familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP), an inherited condition in which many polyps form on the walls of the colon and rectum.","source_span":"Desmoid tumors sometimes occur in children with changes in the adenomatous polyposis coli (APC) gene. Changes in this gene cause familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP). FAP is an inherited condition in which many polyps (growths on mucous membranes) form on the inside walls of the colon and rectum."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","statement":"Infantile fibrosarcoma is found in children aged 4 years and younger, most often in infants, and may be seen on a prenatal ultrasound exam.","source_span":"Infantile fibrosarcoma... is found in children aged 4 years and younger. It most often occurs in infants and may be seen in a prenatal ultrasound exam."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","statement":"Low-grade fibromyxoid sarcoma may come back many years after treatment and spread to the lungs and the lining of the chest cavity wall, so lifelong follow-up is needed.","source_span":"The tumor may come back many years after treatment and spread to the lungs and the lining of the wall of the chest cavity. Lifelong follow-up is needed."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","fact_refs":[1],"question":"Where do soft tissue sarcoma tumors most often form in children?","answer":"In children, soft tissue sarcoma tumors form most often in the arms, legs, or trunk (chest and abdomen)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What genetic change is found in the cells of myxoid liposarcoma, and how is it used?","answer":"Myxoid liposarcoma cells have a translocation genetic change, which is checked for in the tumor cells to diagnose myxoid liposarcoma."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","fact_refs":[2,3],"question":"How does pleomorphic liposarcoma differ from myxoid liposarcoma in grade and treatment response?","answer":"Myxoid liposarcoma is usually low grade and responds well to treatment, while pleomorphic liposarcoma is usually high grade and less likely to respond well to treatment."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","fact_refs":[6],"question":"At what age is infantile fibrosarcoma found, and how might it be detected before birth?","answer":"Infantile fibrosarcoma is found in children aged 4 years and younger, most often in infants, and may be seen on a prenatal ultrasound exam."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What gene change is linked to desmoid tumors in children, and what condition does it cause?","answer":"Desmoid tumors are sometimes linked to changes in the APC gene, which causes familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP), a condition in which many polyps form on the walls of the colon and rectum."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000003_5","fact_refs":[7],"question":"Why is lifelong follow-up needed for patients with low-grade fibromyxoid sarcoma?","answer":"Because the tumor may come back many years after treatment and spread to the lungs and the lining of the chest cavity wall, lifelong follow-up is needed."}
